  <section class="hub-section hub-section-gray">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>How our techs approach commercial refrigeration</h2>
      <p>Five failure modes dominate commercial-refrigeration service: condenser-coil fouling (the most common cause of "not cooling" calls — we clean before quoting parts), condenser-fan motor wear (year 4-7 typical on coastal installs, year 6-9 inland), door-gasket degradation (year 3-5 wear cycle on high-cycle reach-ins), evaporator-fan motor failure, and refrigerant leak or charge drift (EPA 608 work). We're EPA 608 Universal certified with R-290 supplemental for the post-2020 propane-refrigerant generation. Door-gasket replacement is the most common service item we do — gaskets are scheduled-maintenance, not emergency, and we recommend annual inspection on every install.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hub-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is True Manufacturing the same as True Residential?</summary>
          <p>No. True Manufacturing is the Trulaske family Missouri-based commercial refrigeration company. True Residential is a Middleby-owned (acquired 2017) premium home refrigeration brand. Different parts catalogs, different service networks. This category page covers True Manufacturing commercial.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>My reach-in is at 50°F and won't come down. What should I do?</summary>
          <p>Above the 41°F FDA food-safety threshold, move temperature-sensitive inventory immediately. Document the temperature and time for your health-code records. Call us right away — we treat commercial refrigeration as a priority call. Most likely cause: condenser coil fouling forcing the compressor to work past capacity, or a failed condenser fan motor.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do you handle R-290 propane refrigerant on Hoshizaki and Beverage-Air?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Many post-2020 units across the major commercial refrigeration brands transitioned to R-290 (propane) for environmental compliance. R-290 service requires specific certification beyond standard EPA 608 Universal — we hold both.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

